  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Founding and Governance
    
    Crypt-Chancellor Silvcaeclerae-fawn~ founded the deep-tunnel settlement of ☽'slew Nisaemesius~ by leading settlers from Nightfall Shelf into strata no prior expedition had colonized, establishing the first formal governance there under Weal' Clique~, the guild she continues to lead. She was created during the Clever Ice Age, a period whose expansion doctrines drove settlement into places better left unsettled — though in Silvcaeclerae-fawn~'s case, the ice suggests the decision was less doctrine than conviction. The colony she built endures. What it cost her to build it is the subject of the remaining sections.
    
    ## Wartime Role and Practitioner Degradation
    
    During the Orca Incursion, Silvcaeclerae-fawn~ deployed Hush☽ Twilight — a suppressive Nightshelf magic that silences aurora-light and muffles sound through suffocating pressure — to conceal troop movements through deep-tunnel corridors. She is documented as a practitioner of at least seven distinct magical traditions, including ☽Silv-glaciere☽ Arts (the Nightshelf discipline of reading and reshaping the Berg's frozen memory), Fissure☽ Aurora (which fractures aurora-light into usable fire), ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral (which traps moments in crystalline suspension at the cost of the caster's own recollections), Shawl☽ Sun, Star∴eternal, and Veil☽ Glow.
    
    The physical record is severe. Her flippers show Stage IV cold-burn discoloration extending to the secondary joint, beneath older scarring from forge-work and ritual marks in patterns that match no known Nightshelf custom. Ash-gray wrappings wound tight enough around her wrists to leave permanent grooves. She is the most extensively documented case of ☽Silv-glaciere☽ practitioner degradation, her frost-scars consistent with seventh-layer contact — catalogued, with characteristic Nightshelf precision, by the very governance she founded.
    
    Depth-Purveyor ☽'Cilocum, her closest associate, records in his incident notes that her voice post-casting carries a pressure-weight inconsistent with her physical location. He sets out two cups of fire-tea in the Whispered Shrift on nights she does not come. I have encountered this practice elsewhere in the archive. It is not unique to him. It is always recognizable.
    
    ## Ice-Memory Evidence
    
    The ice beneath ☽'slew Nisaemesius~ holds impressions of Silvcaeclerae-fawn~ kneeling in the deepest dark, hands pressed against frozen walls — impressions she does not remember making, measurable 1.4 body-lengths below her resting place. During the Long Dark, when the veil between the living world and ice-memory thins, those who press their flippers against the ice there claim it recites her deeds in voices they recognize. She has declined to confirm or deny the existence of these impressions. I have not attempted independent verification. The Whisper Galleries are not a place I return to lightly.
    
    ## Diplomatic Record
    
    Silvcaeclerae-fawn~ signed the Accord of Beacon Light and Deep Fire on behalf of Weal' Clique~, the joint-stewardship pact with Holdborn (ice-thresh) Aurora-Chartered governing The Beacon Stack. She drew blood upon the ☽'micseleia' Dagger, a Nightshelf relic whose ancestor-bone hilt was reportedly warm to her touch.
    
    ## Cultural Legacy
    
    Nightshelf proverbs have ground her name to a single syllable. *Silv's silence keeps the Berg* is an old saying nobody explains. In miner's cant she is called *the first digger*, and the first digger's debt is the one no ledger records and no audit calls due. The wrappings at her wrists tell half of what she gave. The ice tells the rest — to those willing to go deep enough to read it.
